The purpose of the adjustments made on May 10, 2017, as per Article 16 – Job Vacancies, was:

- To stay competitive in the labour market;
- To attract external applicants, as job titles were misunderstood;
- To ensure sufficient CA (Certified Apprentice) or supervisory coverage per WorkSafe requirements;
- To comply with BC Safety Authority requirements by having Chief Engineers at each location.

These adjustments were made under Article 16.04 (Job Vacancies for Trades and Leadhands), which included removing “and Leadhands” from the heading and rewording the language regarding how vacancies for trades and leadhand positions are filled — specifically to clarify that seniority, qualifications, and ability are considered in filling such vacancies.

The adjustments were formalized in **Letter of Understanding No. 7**, signed by the BC Tree Fruits Cooperative (Employer) and United Food and Commercial Workers International Union, Local 247 (Union), on May 10, 2017.

